  "pride_metadata": {
    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD064001",
      "title": "Analysis of proteins immunoprecipitated with anti-FLAG antibodies from Leishmania donovani promastigotes expressing Cdc45-FLAG or carrying empty vector",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "This study was carried out to identify the interacting partners of Leishmania donovani Cdc45, a protein that is conserved in eukaryotic DNA replication. Accordingly, Cdc45 was expressed in Leishmania promastigotes with a C terminal FLAG tag and whole cell lysates were isolated from these Ld1S transfectant promastigotes. Whole cell lysates were also isolated from promastigotes harbouring empty vector. These lysates were used in immunoprecipitation reactions with anti-FLAG antibodies.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Whole cell extracts were isolated from 1x109 Leishmania donovani promastigotes expressing Cdc45-FLAG using mammalian protein extraction reagent (MPER) mixed with protease inhibitors. Immunoprecipitation was carried out by M2 agarose beads and the bound fraction was eluted by boiling the beads at 100\u00b0C and the eluate was loaded on 10 % SDS gel. Gel pieces were carefully excised out by a surgical blade, immediately after the proteins entered the resolving gel. In-gel destaining using 50% acetonitrile in 25mM ammonium bicarbonate solution was carried out after chopping the gel pieces into smaller pieces. This was followed by in-gel reduction using 10mM DTT in 25mM ammonium bicarbonate and in-gel alkylation using 50mM iodoacetamide in 25mM ammonium bicarbonate. The gel pieces were dehydrated by 100 % acetonitrile, followed by overnight trypsin treatment (2 \u00b5g) at 37\u00b0C. The trypsin digested peptides were extracted with 50% acetonitrile and 0.1% Trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) and the extraction process was repeated thrice. All three rounds of extractions were pooled together and dried by a vacuum concentrator, followed by clean-up using Pierce\u2122 Peptide Desalting Spin Columns (Thermo Fisher Scientific). The dried pellets were re-suspended in 2% acetonitrile solution with 0.1% formic acid, followed by LC-MS analysis using the Thermo Scientific Q-Exactive Orbitrap system coupled with EASY-nLC 1200 (Thermo Fisher Scientific). The re-suspended peptides were loaded on the EASY-Spray PepMap RSLC C18 column with 2\u00b5m size, 75\u00b5m x 50cm and 100 \u00c5 pore size (Thermo Scientific) and separated using a linear gradient of 5% - 45% over 120 minutes (Solvent A - 2% acetonitrile /0.1% formic acid and Solvent B - 80% acetonitrile/0.1% formic acid). For MS1 a resolution of 70000 over 350 to 2000m/z scan range was used with AGC of 3x10-6, and maximum ion transfer time of 50 ms.  For MS2 the resolution of 17500 and 1x10-5AGC was used with maximum ion transfer time of 120 ms. The normalized collision energy unit was set at 27 and DE (dynamic exclusion) was applied with a loop count of 10 and dynamic exclusion time of 50 seconds.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Raw data obtained from LC-MS was analyzed using Proteome Discoverer software (version 2.4.1.15). Peptide sequences in each sample were identified by using the L. donovani proteome library downloaded from TriTrypDB (TriTrpDB-68_LdonovaniBPK282A1_AnnotatedProteins.fasta). Comparative analysis was performed for each of the replicates and candidate proteins were selected on the basis of Log2 fold enrichment.",
